1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,190
Junie: Grandma. The corn is whispering
again.

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:09,314
Radio: Evening, Hollow Creek. This is The
Last Harvest. Part one of three: the corn.

3
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:14,573
Ruth: Corn doesn't whisper, Junie. Corn
rustles.

4
00:00:14,893 --> 00:00:16,154
Junie: Then why did it say my name?

5
00:00:16,493 --> 00:00:18,686
Hank: Ma'am. The corn is walking.

6
00:00:19,006 --> 00:00:20,961
Ruth: Hank. How many?

7
00:00:21,081 --> 00:00:21,859
Hank: ...All of them.

8
00:00:22,179 --> 00:00:24,332
Eli: Nobody panic. I have a plan.

9
00:00:24,452 --> 00:00:26,448
Eli: It's called Scarecrow Two-Point-Oh.

10
00:00:26,768 --> 00:00:28,604
Ruth: Where did you get my radio?

11
00:00:28,724 --> 00:00:30,293
Eli: It's a loan. Mostly.

12
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:32,036
Hank: Why am I carrying it?

13
00:00:32,156 --> 00:00:33,998
Eli: You're tall. And brave.

14
00:00:34,118 --> 00:00:35,117
Hank: I am neither.

15
00:00:35,437 --> 00:00:38,886
Eli: Three. Two. One. Polka.

16
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:39,974
Junie: They're dancing.

17
00:00:40,806 --> 00:00:41,597
Eli: ...They're dancing?!

18
00:00:42,406 --> 00:00:47,964
Ruth: Rule one. Sound leads them. So we
lead the sound.

19
00:00:48,284 --> 00:00:55,544
Ruth: Your grandfather planted this corn.
We pick it. Every ear.

20
00:00:55,664 --> 00:00:56,747
Hank: Every ear.

21
00:00:57,067 --> 00:01:00,451
Radio: ...Hollow Creek, if you can hear
this: the barn door is open.

22
00:01:00,771 --> 00:01:07,341
Radio: Part one of three, The Last Harvest.
Next night: the barn. Follow for part two.

